## Description

The DeepSeek V3.2, V4 and V4.1 encoders render a string parameter value verbatim between its tags (`<｜DSML｜parameter name="..." string="true">value</｜DSML｜parameter>`). The tool instructions they render tell the model to write string values as is. The DSML parser the three share called `.strip()` on every string value, so:

- an edit's `old_string` and `new_string` lost their leading indentation;
- a written file lost its final newline;
- a command lost its trailing space.

